# 12. MUI styling rules

Add strong Cursor guidance for MUI.

The default styling hierarchy should be:

```text
Theme tokens
    ↓
Theme component overrides / variants
    ↓
Reusable @erp/ui components
    ↓
MUI sx/styled for local exceptions
```

Avoid repeated values like:

```text
#1976d2
12px
16px
24px
specific shadows
custom breakpoints
```

throughout feature code when they should be represented by theme tokens.

Use semantic theme concepts.

Examples:

```text
primary
secondary
error
warning
success
info
background.default
background.paper
text.primary
text.secondary
divider
```

Prefer MUI spacing:

```ts
theme.spacing(...)
```

and MUI breakpoints:

```ts
theme.breakpoints.up(...)
theme.breakpoints.down(...)
```

over custom pixel-based responsive logic.

Feature components should not repeatedly invent:

- colors
- spacing scales
- typography
- breakpoints
- border radii
- elevations
- generic loading states
- generic tables
- generic form layout

These concerns should eventually live in the MUI theme or `@erp/ui`.

